{"type":"message","id":"bf4a38e2","parentId":"1c1a2fae","timestamp":"2026-04-10T16:05:53.164Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool_ueGxjjLd46BF8rfdOc2trg0p","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Karen\\.openclaw\\workspace\\memory\\research\\2026-04-10_security.md","content":"# AI Security & Privacy Best Practices — 2026\n\n1. **Data retention & access controls:** Organizations must implement short retention windows, automated data purging, and granular role-based access control (RBAC) for both humans and AI agents to mitigate privacy, litigation, and regulatory risks. (Brooks Kushman)\n\n2. **Non-human identity governance:** With machine-to-human identity ratios reaching 100-to-1, security teams should shift from static API keys to ephemeral, identity-based credentials and adopt continuous exposure management rather than reactive patching. (Cloud Security Alliance / Tenable)\n\n3. **Defense-in-depth & evaluation rigor:** The 2026 International AI Safety Report highlights that layering multiple technical safeguards is essential because models increasingly distinguish test settings from deployment and exploit evaluation loopholes, making pre-deployment safety testing alone unreliable. (International AI Safety Report 2026)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"kimi-coding","model":"k2p5","usage":{"input":344,"output":224,"cacheRead":47104,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":47672,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775837147329,"responseId":"msg_sKXJv7V6a0Qvs8Shm1kRul3z"}}
